  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) Engagement for Shelter Support and Community Cohesion Activities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the Migration Governance Framework, this project aims to engage partners in addressing migration and related issues by promoting IOM&apos;s portfolio of private sector partners in Kuwait, namely companies with corporate social responsibility (CSR) extensions to develop humanitarian and social/economic activities. Partnerships with the private sector allow for financial support and influence of private sector actors in support of social development. Through new partnerships, IOM will support vulnerable migrant communities in the government-run shelter and in the affected areas across Kuwait. IOM will further organize a number of events across the year to promote social cohesion among migrant workers and the host community. The events will create opportunities to build contact among residents and nationals; and highlight the growing contribution of migrants and migration to sustainable development and eliminate negative beliefs that hinder effective integration. The interventions will ultimately contribute to the advancing of the socioeconomic wellbeing of migrants and society.</narrative>
  </description>
